{"Denial cache key concatenates raw fields with underscore and does not include identity type, causing distinct checks to share one negative entry - resource or folder UIDs containing underscores can shift the name and parent boundary, and identities such as anonymous and render service can collide if they use the same UID string": 0.7833011150360107, "When a check is denied, the denial cache returns Allowed: false before the permission cache or DB is consulted - if the user is granted access or creates the dashboard/folder during the 30-second cache window, the next check still skips the DB refresh path and incorrectly denies access": 0.8216500282287598}